v4.115.0 — examples/async_http_demo.mn native run evidence
==========================================================

Date: 2026-04-14

## Compile + link

  $ python3 -m mapanare emit-llvm examples/async_http_demo.mn -o /tmp/ahd.ll
  $ llvm-as /tmp/ahd.ll -o /dev/null        # no output — valid
  $ clang /tmp/ahd.ll -L runtime/native -lmapanare_rt -lpthread -lm -ldl -o /tmp/async_http_demo

## Run

  $ rm -f /tmp/async_http_demo_summary.txt
  $ /tmp/async_http_demo
  fetched bytes=540
  pipeline   bytes=540 marker=1
  summary file path: /tmp/async_http_demo_summary.txt

  $ cat /tmp/async_http_demo_summary.txt
  bytes=540 marker=1

## What this proves

1. http_get() builtin lowers to __mn_http_get in libmapanare_rt.a,
   which makes a real TCP connection to example.com (port 80) and
   returns 540 bytes — the Example Domain page.
2. The async pipeline (body_bytes → has_marker → write_summary)
   runs over the fetched body through block_on.
3. has_marker correctly detects "Example Domain" substring
   (marker=1).
4. write_summary writes 19 bytes to /tmp/async_http_demo_summary.txt
   from inside an awaited async fn — real disk I/O from inside an
   async pipeline.

## Behaviour on network failure

If the sandbox blocks outbound TCP, http_get returns an empty
String. The program prints "network unreachable: http_get
returned empty String" and exits with code 0 (not a crash) —
deterministic in CI.

## Follow-ups

Same Sh.9 workarounds apply: fetch synchronously before block_on,
fold write's return into the pipeline's encoding so DCE does not
eliminate the side-effecting call.
